  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1126 AM CDT Tue May 26 2026\n\nJust a few more days of dreary rain and we will be thrust into a \ndrier pattern starting on the weekend. Notice I said driER not DRY. \nMoisture and instability will linger as we struggle to adjust under \na 500mb ridge that begins to flip our pattern on Thursday. \nThunderstorms remain a possibility both Thursday and Friday, but \nagain, no organized severe weather is possible. By the weekend, \nthings will begin to really flip as cold front pushes south through \nMiddle Tennessee. While this front won't do much temperature wise, \nit will dry up some of the moisture, leading to lesser POPs in the \nnext work week. Some rain has been nice for our drought, but it's \ntime for more sunshine in Middle Tennessee, and hopefully we'll get \nsome of that.",
